#      power, so the search locks onto whatever un-whitened band happens to be loudest
#    - (d) The matched-filter code has a bug
#
# 2. `matched_filter_snr` combines a cosine-phase and a sine-phase correlation as
#    `sqrt(zc**2 + zs**2)` rather than using `zc` alone. Why?
#    - (a) The signal's phase at arrival is not known in advance, and a single fixed-phase
#      template would score far lower whenever the true signal's phase happened to be close
#      to that template's own zero-crossing
#    - (b) It doubles the effective sample rate
#    - (c) It removes the need for whitening
#    - (d) It is only a normalisation convenience with no effect on detection
